          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            How often to seal marble is a question the stone answers better than any schedule. Test busy areas every few months and quieter ones twice a year, reseal only where water soaks in, and keep cleaners pH-neutral so the sealer lasts as long as it can. A good impregnator from our <a href="/best-marble-sealer/">marble sealer guide</a> stretches those intervals further.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Expect kitchen counters, especially near the sink, to need attention most often, and do not mistake etching for failed sealer. Polish etches, poultice stains, and keep a note of when you sealed what, and within a year you will know your marble's real rhythm.
          </p>
